  "body": "This will be used by w3c/manifest#1069 to recommend that user agents set this correctly when fetching the manifest without a document.\n\nYou can see the context in [this preview](https://pr-preview.s3.amazonaws.com/mgiuca/manifest/pull/1069.html#processing-the-manifest-without-a-document):\n\n> Additionally, the user agent SHOULD ensure that the bodyBytes data was fetched with a [CORS Request](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#cors-request) whose [Origin](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#http-origin) is linkOrigin, and that its [credentials mode](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-credentials-mode) is set to the [**CORS settings attribute credentials mode**](https://whatpr.org/html/8754/urls-and-fetching.html#cors-settings-attribute-credentials-mode) for linkElement's [crossorigin](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#attr-link-crossorigin) attribute. (The HTML steps automatically ensure this.)\n\nWould it be OK to export this definition?\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9204/urls-and-fetching.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 24, 2023, 5:46 AM UTC (3702d07)\">/urls-and-fetching.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/9204/9dc8962...3702d07/urls-and-fetching.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 24, 2023, 5:46 AM UTC (3702d07)\">diff</a> )",
